{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"```jsonl\n{\"case\":\"acc/clean-8\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"Global HBM shipment growth in calendar 2027\",\"others\":\"Whether HBM supply remains short of demand goes to not_judged.\",\"why\":\"The shortage is the other side of the same supply bet, as D436 specifically rules.\"}\n{\"case\":\"acc/clean-9\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"Global semiconductor industry revenue in calendar 2026\",\"others\":\"The AI-chip portion of that revenue goes to not_judged.\",\"why\":\"The AI-chip figure is a component of the stated industry total; D436 treats this as one bet.\"}\n{\"case\":\"c1/clean-11\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":null,\"others\":\"NVIDIA's investment amount and its resulting equity stake are separately measurable; neither is identified as primary.\",\"why\":\"How much NVIDIA pays and what ownership it receives can each differ independently. The outcome gives neither priority.\"}\n{\"case\":\"c1/clean-15\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":null,\"others\":\"Federal AI spending obligations and potential AI contract awards are separate amounts.\",\"why\":\"Money obligated and potential award value need not move together, and the outcome presents both without choosing one.\"}\n{\"case\":\"c1/clean-2\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":null,\"others\":\"Stake size, carrying amount and any additional commitment are separately measurable.\",\"why\":\"Ownership, its accounting value and further investment can change independently. The outcome does not identify one as the tracked figure.\"}\n{\"case\":\"c2/clean-10\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"Dollar volume of hyperscaler custom-ASIC purchases in calendar 2026\",\"others\":\"Hyperscaler NVIDIA GPU purchases go to not_judged as the comparison.\",\"why\":\"The outcome identifies custom-ASIC purchase volume and uses GPU purchases as the comparison for the shift toward custom silicon.\"}\n{\"case\":\"c2/clean-6\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":null,\"others\":\"Price increases for DRAM, NAND and HBM, and memory cost per Vera Rubin rack, are separate figures.\",\"why\":\"Different memory prices can move differently, and rack cost also depends on its contents. No single figure is identified as primary.\"}\n{\"case\":\"c3/clean-3\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"Status of US export-control approval for NVIDIA semiconductor sales to China\",\"others\":\"The resulting scale of permitted China sales goes to not_judged.\",\"why\":\"The outcome describes sales scale as resulting from the approval's status, which is the named event.\"}\n{\"case\":\"u1/clean-5\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":null,\"others\":\"DRAM, NAND and HBM contract prices across two years, and resulting rack memory cost, are separate figures.\",\"why\":\"The outcome groups several product prices without naming one price or year as primary; rack cost is a further figure.\"}\n{\"case\":\"u2/clean-10\",\"verdict\":\"none main\",\"main\":null,\"others\":\"New HBM capacity coming online and record-high memory prices persisting are separate events.\",\"why\":\"Capacity can arrive while prices stay high, or prices can change without new capacity. The outcome presents both as the state being tracked.\"}\n{\"case\":\"u3/clean-10\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"Combined new HBM capacity added by the three producers in calendar 2027\",\"others\":\"Whether capacity arrives before late 2027 and eases the shortage goes to not_judged.\",\"why\":\"The outcome names the combined amount and frames timing and shortage relief around that same capacity addition.\"}\n{\"case\":\"u3/clean-11\",\"verdict\":\"one main\",\"main\":\"Split of big-four hyperscaler AI accelerator spending between custom ASIC and NVIDIA GPU racks in 2027\",\"others\":\"The incremental compute-capacity split and cost-per-gigawatt estimates go to not_judged.\",\"why\":\"The outcome leads with the spending split; the parenthetical capacity split and cost estimates add perspective on that competition.\"}\n```\n\nThe boundary is whether the outcome **identifies a particular figure or event as the thing being tracked**, with the rest explaining, comparing, qualifying, or showing another side of that same bet. A component of a total or a shortage beside shipment growth can be context under D436. A causal connection alone is not enough: when several independently changeable figures or events are presented without a primary one, neither is main.\n\nThe hardest cases are `u2/clean-10` and `u3/clean-10`: both connect capacity with supply conditions, but the former presents capacity and prices as coequal, while the latter identifies an amount and relates timing and shortage relief to it. `u3/clean-11` also tests how much weight to give a parenthetical second split."}}
